# lilJack sixel terminal — xterm-256color plus the Sxl (sixel) flag.
#
# tmux gates sixel on the ATTACH CLIENT's TERM carrying the `Sxl` boolean
# capability (tty-features.c: tty_feature_sixel_capabilities = {"Sxl"}), checked
# via tigetflag. No entry on the box advertises it, so tmux substitutes the
# literal "SIXEL IMAGE (WxH)" placeholder. This entry is xterm-256color EXACTLY,
# plus one boolean flag: every string/number capability that controls colour,
# keys and line drawing is inherited unchanged, so a terminal that never draws a
# sixel renders byte-identically to today.
#
# `use=xterm-256color` inherits the whole entry; `Sxl,` adds only the flag.
# Compiled with `tic -x` (extended capabilities) into the lilJack cache; the
# attach client falls back to plain xterm-256color if tic is unavailable.
xterm-256color-sixel|tmux sixel passthrough terminal,
	use=xterm-256color,
	Sxl,
